{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Biographies"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Luciano Pavarotti"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 15}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe jobs and careers in social contexts appropriate for the interlocutor."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le15ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Simple Past Passive"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use an active structure when you want the \u2018doer' of the action to be the subject. </br> You use a passive structure when you want the \u2018receiver' of the action to be the subject. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Active sentence = People (subject)<span class=\"strong\"> regarded </span> Luciano Pavarotti (object) as as one of the foremost talents in the music world."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Passive sentence = Luciano Pavarotti (subject) was<span class=\"strong\"> regarded </span>as as one of the foremost talents in the music world (<span class=\"underline\">by people</span> = agent)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "It is not necessary to mention the object in a passive sentence. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often choose the passive form when you want to talk about an action but are not so interested in saying who or what does/did it. Passives without <span class=\"italic\">agents</span> (the doers) are common in biographies. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of the be verb followed by the past participle. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "This is the form of the Simple Past passive:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "subject + was/were + past participle"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">was acclaimed</span> for the beauty of his voice.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Pavarotti was brought up in rural Italy by his working-class parents (his father was a baker and his mother a factory worker)."}, {"type": "example", "content": "His father was also an amateur musician, and it was suggested that he could have become a successful tenor in his own right."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The whole family was crowded into a small, two-bedroom apartment. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "In his later years, Pavarotti was known as a philanthropist."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He was lauded for his humanitarian efforts in raising money for the United Nations following conflicts in Guatemala, Kosovo, Iraq, and Bosnia."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Speculation About the Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use modals to talk about degrees of certainty and speculate about things in the past. </br>You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to describe degrees of certainty.</br>You can use modals with the Present Perfect to talk about the possibility of a past event that is not clear in the present context."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">He was acclaimed for the beauty of his voice, and many believe that he <span class=\"strong\">may have been</span> the preeminent tenor of his generation.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart for the meanings of modals when speculating about the past:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Modal Phrase </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Meaning  </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Must have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is very likely\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"May have</br>Might have </br>Could have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is possible\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">May have </span>has a slightly stronger meaning that <span class=\"italic\">might have</span> or <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>.</li><li> You can add <span class=\"strong\">not </span>to make a negative speculation (<span class=\"italic\">It <span class=\"strong\">may not have been </span>true</span>).</li></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "His frugal upbringing must have influenced the generosity he displayed in his later years. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "His father was also an amateur musician, and it was suggested that he could have become a successful tenor in his own right. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Many believe that he may have been the preeminent tenor of his generation."}, {"type": "example", "content": " Imagine, the great Pavarotti might have become a professional footballer!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stardom"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the state of being famous"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: At the height of his stardom, Luciano Pavarotti was known throughout the world. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about jobs and fame. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "foremost"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the most prominent in rank; the best"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Luciano Pavarotti was regarded as as one of the foremost talents in the music world. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "preeminent"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "more important or better than others"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Many believe that he may have been the preeminent tenor of his generation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to laud"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to praise"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He was lauded for his humanitarian efforts."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob02aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "overnight sensation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone who becomes famous very quickly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: For all of his natural talent, Pavarotti was not an overnight sensation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob02aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "household name"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who is well known by the public"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He began his musical career in 1961, and within a decade he had become a household name."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob02aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "working-class"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " those who usually work with their hands and are paid by the hour"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Pavarotti was brought up in rural Italy by his working-class parents (his father was a baker and his mother a factory worker). "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "baker"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who makes bread and cakes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: His father was a baker so he always had fresh bread at home."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "philanthropist"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who helps the poor, often by giving them money"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In his later years, Pavarotti was known as a philanthropist. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob02aud10"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "humanitarian"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "attempting to improve human welfare or reduce suffering"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He was lauded for his humanitarian efforts in raising money for the United Nations."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le15ob02aud11"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Create a title for your organization."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a mission statement."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Outline four ways in which your organization will help people."}, {"type": "text", "conte