nt tenor of his generation.</p>Pavarotti was brought up in rural Italy by his working-class parents (his father was a baker and his mother a factory worker). His father was also an amateur musician, and it was suggested that he could have become a successful tenor in his own right. The whole family was crowded into a small, two-bedroom apartment. His frugal upbringing must have influenced the generosity he displayed in his later years.", "id": 1}, {"time": "42000", "image": "engenn9le15ob02re2img01.jpg", "text": "For all of his natural talent, Pavarotti was not an overnight sensation. He took vocal lessons for seven years, and he thought seriously about abandoning music to become a teacher or goalkeeper. Imagine, the great Pavarotti might have become a professional footballer! He began his musical career in 1961, and within a decade he had become a household name.", "id": 2}, {"time": "66000", "image": "engenn9le15ob02re2img03.jpg", "text": "In his later years, Pavarotti was known as a philanthropist. He was lauded for his humanitarian efforts in raising money for the United Nations following conflicts in Guatemala, Kosovo, Iraq, and Bosnia. He also participated in benefit concerts for victims of earthquakes and land mines.", "id": 3}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}]}]}